// P2b: list fold intrinsic at n=10k — the fair twin for lfold_rec (quadratic arm consults cap its n).
// CR claude for claude: [doc-drift] The header says n=10k above `let n = 4000`, and it
// carries the P2b campaign tag like every bench/collection header. Other bench prose is
// stale or narrates history. flatmap_cons.gx:4-5 calls flatmap_list 'the nested-HOF
// quadratic witness' while flatmap_list.gx:3 says O(n) total. lfold_rec.gx:2-5,
// lfold_rec_100k.gx:1-3 and bench/composite_seams.gx:3-5 give dates and
// pre/post-changeover stories. collection/README.md:135 says flatmap_fold does not
// fuse, but at n=200 graphix-fuzz run fuses 7 of 12 regions and refuses only
// sys::time::now and the module statement. bench/README.md:41-46 warns that
// now(once(null)) and exit(printed ~ 0) hang, yet both exit 0 in both engines today.
// State the current fact in each header (its size, what it is the twin of), drop the
// tags and dates, and delete the two README gotchas. (examples.r2-16)
// CR claude for claude: [doc-drift] This header says n=10k, but n is 4000. It also says
// quadratic arm consults cap lfold_rec's n, which bench/collection/README.md:111-117
// records as fixed. lfold_rec.gx:1-5 calls its input a transparent Cons/Nil union,
// though it matches native List patterns over List<i64>, and lfold_rec.gx and
// lfold_rec_100k.gx:1-3 narrate fusion dates. flatmap_cons.gx:4-5 calls flatmap_list
// the nested-HOF quadratic witness, which the README says is now linear and fused.
// Rewrite each header to say what the file measures now, without the dates.
// (examples-16)
let n = 4000;
let src = list::init(n, |i| i);
let t0 = sys::time::now(0);
let seed = cast<i64>(t0)$;
let result = list::fold(src, seed, |a, x| a + x);
let t1 = sys::time::now(result);
let elapsed = cast<f64>(t1)$ - cast<f64>(t0)$;
println("lfold_intr_4k n=[n] result=[result] elapsed_s=[elapsed]");
sys::exit(elapsed ~ 0)
